      "writtenOn": "2023-10-26T20:49:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The client should be passing us in the features they enabled. In Vulkan you first query the physical device for what features they support (like you\u0027re doing here). Then when you create the VkDevice you pass those Features back in. But you can disable any feature you don\u0027t want even if the physical device says it supports it. The features are on the VulkanBackendContext, we just haven\u0027t passed them into the creation of VulkanCaps yet.\n\nSee how we check for ycbcr support in Ganesh.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 114,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 117,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "e0bb9391d1b513f7c2a70b29b86fc2c1c71dfb2e",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "866febe4_8a906054",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/vk/VulkanCaps.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 19
      },
      "lineNbr": 117,
      "author": {
        "id": 18914
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-03T17:09:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ah, I see. Thank you for the explanation. I added piping for `VulkanSharedContext` to communicate `VulkanBackendContext`\u0027s physical device feature information provided by the client down into `VulkanCaps` creation. \n\nI also moved the `get_extension_feature_struct(...)` function from `GrVkCaps`--\u003e`VulkanUtilsPriv` so it can be shared b/w graphite and ganesh to query `VkPhysicalDeviceFeatures2` for extension feature structures. For now, graphite only uses it for YCbCr conversion info, but having that helper available should be beneficial later on as we want to query for more enabled Vulkan features within graphite.\n\nAlso, to be clear, \"In Vulkan you first query the physical device for what features they support (like you\u0027re doing here)\" - the client will be performing this query themselves (like we do when we set up our own internal features for testing in `VkTestUtils`) when creating a VkDevice before they pass that feature struct to us? We do not need to verify that a feature they enabled/requested is actually supported by the physical device we were provided and are using?",
      "parentUuid": "b5a2ac69_df0891e5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 114,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 117,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "e0bb9391d1b513f7c2a70b29b86fc2c1c71dfb2e",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "574aa2a3_dc8260bf",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/vk/VulkanCaps.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 19
      },
      "lineNbr": 117,
      "author": {
        "id": 5036
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-03T19:55:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Correct, we don\u0027t need to query the physical device. We just trust the features the client tells us are enable.",
      "parentUuid": "866febe4_8a906054",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 114,
        "startChar": 4,
