      "message": "Good question - Because of this change (https://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/754316 ;\nrelevant comment documentation: https://skia.googlesource.com/skia.git/+/refs/heads/main/include/gpu/graphite/BackendTexture.h#126) \nwhere Vulkan backend textures now have a VulkanAlloc member attribute which can have a real OR 0 handle to backend memory. \n\nIn the case where `VulkanAlloc`\u0027s `fBackendMemory` is \u003d 0, meaning the VkImage was already created and will be destroyed by the caller (example: `GraphiteVulkanWindowContext::createBuffers`), we should not attempt to free the image memory. The DestroyImage call should also be within this if statement, so I fixed that.\n\nIn the case of the `GraphiteVulkanWindowContext`, for example, the vkDestroySwapchainKHR command destroys the VkImage handles (https://registry.khronos.org/vulkan/specs/1.3-extensions/man/html/vkDestroySwapchainKHR.html), so we should not attempt to do so here.",
